# What travels and what does not.
#
# Travels: the manuscript sources, the workstream records, the reproducibility
# scripts, and the small JSON each run writes. Those are the evidence and the
# means to regenerate it, and they are worth reading in a diff.
#
# Also travels, since 2026-09-14: the converted graphs the results were computed
# from, under w2/graphs/ and w5/graphs/. All 42 of them weigh 352 KB together --
# they are the direct evidence a reader can point at, and nothing about them is
# large. Both the discovery run (pre-correction converter) and the final run are
# kept, because the paper reports a difference between them.
#
# Stays on the VM: run metrics, working conversion trees and LaTeX
# intermediates. The metrics are timing logs rather than evidence, the working
# trees are regenerable, and a git history of either is noise.

# --- converted RDF and conversion working state -------------------------------
w2/conv/
w2/out/
w4/conv/
w4/out/
**/run_metrics/
**/.intermediate/
*.nt
*.nt.gz
*.nt.br
*.hdt
*.hdt.index*
*.cottas
*.cottas.gz
*.ttl.gz
*.vcf.gz
*.bcf
vcf_core_reviewed/

# --- LaTeX build products -----------------------------------------------------
.build/
*.aux
*.bbl
*.blg
*.fdb_latexmk
*.fls
*.log
*.out
*.toc
*.synctex.gz
pdfa.xmpi

# --- packaging ----------------------------------------------------------------
VCF-Core-SWAT4HCLS-2027*.zip

# --- python -------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/

# --- deliberately kept, despite the rules above -------------------------------
# The exported PDFs are the submission artifacts, so they stay tracked.
!main_long.pdf
!main_short.pdf
# Every generated JSON under w2/ is a recorded result, not an intermediate.
!w2/generated/
!w2/generated/**
# The graphs each result was computed from. Small, and the evidence itself.
!w2/graphs/
!w2/graphs/**
!w4/generated/
!w4/generated/**
!w5/generated/
!w5/generated/**
!w5/graphs/
!w5/graphs/**
